  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project by UNICEF will provide integrated life-saving comprehensive packages of services to at least 390,000 vulnerable population members, including 67,000 children and 2,000 persons with disabilities, as well as their caregivers and communities in need in Rakhine State and Magway region. These areas, rated high priority in the HRP 2023, are severely impacted by conflict and are deprived of life-saving and essential services.&#xa0;lt/pgtltpgtRakhine state has the worst nutrition and health status in Myanmar, and the demand has only increased since cyclone Mocha ripped across coastal townships on May 14, 2023. According to the Nutrition Information Management System (NIS), Rakhine is home to 91 percent of the country&apos;s severe acute malnutrition (SAM) caseload. Eighty to one hundred percent of the health facilities in the affected townships were either completely or partially damaged.&#xa0;ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtTogether with its non-governmental partners, such as local organizations, faith-based organizations, and youth organizations, UNICEF will endeavor to deliver a package of life-saving interventions to children, caretakers, and the communities in which they live who are impacted by violence.lt/pgtltpgtltspangtltbrgtlt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspangtThe proposed plt/spangtltspangtroject will complement UNICEF&#x2019;s ongoing support for humanitarian response and scale up nutrition, health, and child protection services through partners to have timely responses and ensure the availability of critical social services in those areas, including:&#xa0;lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgt- The provision of life-saving preventive and curative nutrition services, including nutrition screening and treatment of children with severe acute malnutrition, maternal, infant, and young child feeding (MIYCF) counselling, and multiple micronutrient supplementations to children and pregnant lactation women coordination as the sector lead of the nutrition cluster and the provision of supplies to scale up services.&#xa0;Interventions will also be extended to support the renovation of health facilities that Cyclone Mocha damaged.lt/pgtltpgtltspangtltbrgtlt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspangt- UNICEF Child Protection will&#xa0;support with the Provision of Mental Health and Psychosocial (MHPSS) services family tracing and reunification (FTR) prevention of killing and maiming of children through Explosive Ordinance Risk Education (EORE) provision of case management, alternative care, referral to specialized services and other basic services prevention and mitigation of gender-based violence, physical and sexual abuse, and exploitation through sensitization and awareness raising.lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
